<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fruela II of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 875–925</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Fruela II of León</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fruela II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 910 and of León from 924 until his death in 925. A son of Alfonso III the Great, he received Asturias when his father's realm was divided among his sons, and on the death of his brother Ordoño II he took the throne of León, reuniting the inheritance. His short reign was followed by a succession dispute among his nephews and sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fruela-ii-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Fruela II of Asturias" width="273" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fruela2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The realm was divided among his sons: García I took León, the new centre of royal power, Ordoño II took Galicia, and <b>Fruela II</b> took Asturias itself.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 910 Alfonso III was deposed by his sons, and his realm was divided: García I took the lands south of the mountains, centred on León, Ordoño received Galicia and <b>Fruela</b> Asturias.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
